<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Molla Panah Vagif</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1717–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Vagif</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Molla Panah Vagif was an Azerbaijani poet and statesman who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the Karabakh Khanate under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-khalil-khan">Ibrahim Khalil Khan</a>. His lyric poems, written in a simple style close to spoken Azerbaijani, made him one of the founders of modern Azerbaijani poetry. He was executed in 1797 during the turmoil that followed the assassination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> ruler Agha Mohammad Khan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/molla-panah-vagif.jpg" alt="Molla Panah Vagif" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of Azerbaijan/Azermarka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamps_of_Azerbaijan,_2014-1186.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
